,"vote":"no"},{"name":"Susan Templeman","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10873","person_slug":"susan-templeman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tania Lawrence","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10981","person_slug":"tania-lawrence","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tanya Plibersek","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10513","person_slug":"tanya-plibersek","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ted O'Brien","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10866","person_slug":"ted-obrien","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Terry Young","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10933","person_slug":"terry-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Burke","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tracey Roberts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10994","person_slug":"tracey-roberts","vote":"no"},{"name":"Warren Entsch","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10203","person_slug":"warren-entsch","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zaneta Mascarenhas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10999","person_slug":"zaneta-mascarenhas","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zoe Daniel","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10979","person_slug":"zoe-daniel","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zoe McKenzie","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10976","person_slug":"zoe-mckenzie","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Treasury Laws Amendment (Tax Accountability and Fairness) Bill 2023 - Consideration in Detail - Petroleum resource rent tax","noes":65,"question":"The majority voted against [amendments](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debate/?id=2024-03-18.48.2) introduced by Hume MP [Angus Taylor](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/hume/angus_taylor) (Liberal), which means they failed. ### What do these amendments do? Mr Taylor [explained that](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debate/?id=2024-03-18.48.2): > *These amendments seek to split the Treasury Laws Amendment (Tax Accountability and Fairness) Bill 2023 in order to deal with the PwC schedules separately to the [PRRT](https://www.ato.gov.au/businesses-and-organisations/gst-excise-and-indirect-taxes/petroleum-resource-rent-tax) [petroleum resource rent tax] measure. The important point about this is that these issues are completely different. On the one hand, we have the PwC and Tax Practitioners Board issue, which rightly should be considered by this place. It's a very important issue in the integrity of our tax and tax administration system. On the other hand, we have the PRRT. These are completely different issues.* This amendment would have omitted the petroleum resource rent tax provisions from the bill. ### Amendment text > *(1) Clause 2, page 2 (table item 4), omit the table item.* > > *(2) Schedule 5, page 32 (line 1) to page 38 (line 23), omit the Schedule.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-8720","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2024-03-18/6"}
